{"ts": 1791256584.199998, "type": "step", "step": 17, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "You\u2019re stuck on the eval part, so let\u2019s pin down the two ideas that matter most for the writeup:\n1) **pass@k vs pass^k**: pass@k means at least one of k attempts succeeds; pass^k means **all** k attempts succeed. For a Friday build, reliability is closer to pass^k.\n2) **proxy vs direct measures**: if you measure something indirect (like a quiz score), that\u2019s a proxy. If you measure the actual goal (like retention later), that\u2019s closer to a direct measure.\n\nQuick check: in your own words, which one should you report if the build needs consistency across runs, and why?", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: nice, I think I see it now\n[activity] t=0 messages 2m", "t": 2, "activity": [{"t": 0, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.2930966219605771, "pomdp": 0.2930966219605771, "pass_k": 0.3575089192721116}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 1.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.6914904699846633, "motivation": 0.7582565640937223, "reliance": 0.4841130265401042, "persistence": 0.3650501251360847, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.25123269521051517, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.32885785171436704, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
